/-
Johnson/G/LayoutLit.lean: the layout of a request's arrays at the full size, written out whole: for
each of the 25 segments of the proof file's first chain its arrays, each with its name, the number
of the oracle message that holds it, its rows and columns, and the rectangles in which it is laid
(`ReqLayout`, `ReqArray`, `LaidBlock`, OnBytes/Params/Items.lean). Data alone: five definitions.

The 25 segments have four layouts: 40 arrays and 1013 rectangles stand for 227 and 5419. One stands
at segment 0, one at the segments 1, 3, …, 23, one at 2, 4, …, 22, one at 24. By the list of the
segments' sorts (`linksFull`, Johnson/Desc/Sound/AtDriver.lean: twelve times layers and attention,
then the head) these are the first segment of layers, attention, the later segments of layers, and
the head: whence the four names.

Whence. Made by program from a print of the field `layout` of the proof file's first chain's
parameters, as read back, at the stored full-size public files (`VerifierAndGoals.storedPublicFiles`). The printed value
was computed by the public part of the IOP as written in Lean (`ProofFile.pureRoad.pub`,
Johnson/Desc/ProofFile/OnlineDescriptionPublicPart.lean), whose planner is a copy of the library's
(Johnson/Desc/ProofFile/PlanPlain.lean), not the library's own `planned`. The print: Lean's
evaluator, the type's derived `Repr`, 2117124 bytes, parsed whole. That the program wrote what the
print says is held by unrolling this file's five definitions and comparing them with the parsed
print, value by value, by program. A second evaluation, by the library's own planner at every build,
is Johnson/G/LayoutLitGuard.lean. The head of Johnson/Desc/ProofFile/PlanPlain.lean says how far
the copy is from the library's planner. No theorem says that a planner returns this value.

Definitions. `layoutFirst`, `layoutAtt`, `layoutLay`, `layoutHead`: the four. `layoutFull`: the 25
in their order.

A rectangle's nine fields, in the order of `LaidBlock`: firstI, firstC, firstRow, firstPlace, bitsI,
bitsC, rowBits, placeBits, iIsLow.


-/
